00:24:56.760 --> 00:25:03.640
and judging criteria will be creativity, cohesion,&nbsp;
and likelihood to produce dynamic gameplan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:09.600
And—this time there’s a prize. The creator of each&nbsp;
of the top decks will receive a Haunted One alter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:09.600 --> 00:25:15.320
hand-painted by my friend Mechacatten who did the&nbsp;
art for my channel banner and profile picture. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:15.320 --> 00:25:19.400
that sounds up your alley, you can find more&nbsp;
info about the challenge in my discord server,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:19.400 --> 00:25:24.880
and you’ll want to submit a deck&nbsp;
by noon PST on Tuesday the 21st.

00:25:24.880 --> 00:25:27.880
As always I want to thank my patrons for&nbsp;
supporting what I do here, allowing me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:27.880 --> 00:25:31.800
to make high effort videos like this one without&nbsp;
needing to worry too much about how they’ll fare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:31.800 --> 00:25:36.840
in the algorithm. Submissions for this month’s&nbsp;
deck review will run until the end of tomorrow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:36.840 --> 00:25:40.520
so if you want to have a chance at getting your&nbsp;
deck reviewed by me, you can check that out. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:40.520 --> 00:25:44.920
you want more of me and don’t want to pay money, I&nbsp;
was on an episode of the Magic Mirror Podcast that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:44.920 --> 00:25:49.360
should be releasing around the same time as this&nbsp;
video, and there I go further into my feelings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:49.360 --> 00:25:55.160
about tutors along with my two co-hosts. A link&nbsp;
to that is in the description. Alright, bye now.

